%N A398815 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes that are reducible as a flow graph rooted at no node.
%C A398815 The everywhere-irreducible strong digraphs: the deficit a(n) = A003030(n) - A401321(n) between all strong digraphs and those reducible from at least one root (the at-least-one-valid-header count), i.e. N_0 in the valid-header distribution N_j of that entry.
%C A398815 The smallest example is the complete digraph on 3 nodes (the unique one at n = 3); irreducibility from every root needs every root to see some multiple-entry strongly connected subgraph.
%C A398815 All digraphs here have no self-loops.
%D A398815 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A398815 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A398815 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A398815 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A398815 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398815/b398815.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..30</a>
%H A398815 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A398815 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A398815 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Python program (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A398815 a(n) = A003030(n) - A401321(n).
%F A398815 a(n) = A003030(n) - Sum_{s=1..n} (-1)^(s+1) * binomial(n,s) * R_s(n), where R_s(n) counts strong digraphs reducible from every root in one fixed s-subset of the vertices.
%o A398815 (Python)
%o A398815 # Save the three linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A398815 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A398815 from valid_header_elections import valid_header_sequence
%o A398815 valid_header_sequence("labeled_strong_no_valid_header", 16)
%Y A398815 Cf. A003030 (all strong digraphs), A401321, A397470, A400123.
%K A398815 nonn,new
